XZ Utils for OpenVMS
====================

This is XZ Utils @VERSION@ built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the
unmodified release plus the patches in the vms-xz project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-xz

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  XZ Utils is free software; liblzma and the tools are under the
0BSD licence; see COPYING.  The manual is XZ.TXT; XZ.1, XZDEC.1 and
LZMAINFO.1 are the manual pages.

What is installed
-----------------
    XZ$ROOT:[BIN]XZ.EXE, XZDEC.EXE, LZMAINFO.EXE
    XZ$ROOT:[LIB]LIBLZMA.OLB        the library (liblzma)
    XZ$ROOT:[INCLUDE]LZMA.H, LZMA_*.H
    XZ$ROOT:[DOC]                   this file, COPYING, NEWS, the manual
    XZ$ROOT:[000000]XZ$SETUP.COM   defines the commands
    SYS$STARTUP:XZ$STARTUP.COM      defines XZ$ROOT

Setting up
----------
The kit installs XZ$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define XZ$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:XZ$STARTUP.COM

Each user (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone) then defines the commands:

    $ @XZ$ROOT:[000000]XZ$SETUP.COM

Using it
--------
    $ xz "-k" file.txt              ! file.txt.xz, keeping file.txt
    $ unxz file.txt.xz              ! xz -d
    $ xzcat file.txt.xz             ! to SYS$OUTPUT
    $ xz "-l" file.txt.xz           ! list it

xz also reads .lzma and .lz files.  A name like file.txt.xz needs an ODS-5
disk.  This build is single-threaded.  The highest presets need much
memory: -9 needs about 674 MiB to compress, more than a default PGFLQUOTA
allows ("not enough core"); the default -6 needs about 94 MiB.

Text and binary files
---------------------
A VMS text file (variable-length or VFC records) is compressed as text:
its records become lines ending in LF, as on Unix, so the compressed file
can be unpacked anywhere.  Decompressing gives a Stream_LF file with the
same lines.  Any other file (stream, fixed-length records: executables,
kits, binary data) is compressed byte for byte.

Using the library
-----------------
Compile with /INCLUDE=XZ$ROOT:[INCLUDE] and link with
XZ$ROOT:[LIB]LIBLZMA.OLB/LIBRARY.  The library is compiled /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED); its
header declares the API so, so a program compiled with any /NAMES links
with it.

On VMS lzma.h includes its subheaders as LZMA_*.H, all in [INCLUDE].

Exit status
-----------
Under DCL a failed run exits with an error-severity status, so ON ERROR and
IF .NOT. $STATUS work; the exit code N is ($STATUS .AND. %X7F8) / 8.  Under
a GNV shell, $? is the exit code as on Unix.

Upper-case options and batch jobs
---------------------------------
Under the TRADITIONAL DCL parse style DCL upper-cases the unquoted parts of
a command and the C run-time library passes them to the program in lower
case.  Batch jobs use TRADITIONAL even when interactive logins are set to
EXTENDED.  Quote options with capitals, use the long forms, or start the
procedure with

    $ SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED
